<p style="text-align: center; line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;" align="center"><span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;"><strong>Piggybacking </strong></span></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"><strong>JHC Employees  </strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"><strong>What is Tailgating? Tailgating occurs when an authorized individual permits others to follow behind without showing or registering proper authorization and gain access to a secure area.</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"><strong>Tailgating is a function of both the attitude of the individual and the corporate culture towards adherence to security measures. The impacts of tailgating affect both the business and personnel including; theft of equipment and intellectual property; workplace violence and safety.</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"><strong>We as security officers work together with management and City Security to maintain a secure environment for all tenants and visitors. </strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"><strong>We need your help to maintain the level of security. At times that has become a challenge when tenants allow others to enter the building without knowledge of the person's access status. We ask all tenants to please not allow Piggybacking in the building for everyone's safety.</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"><strong>If you happen to encounter an individual trying to gain access to any of the building's entrances, please refer them to the main entrance. The same applies to deliveries, food deliveries and small items deliveries. Please send them to the front desk to allow security to handle it.</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"><strong>Thank you for your cooperation. Respectfully,</strong></p>
<p style="line-height: 1.4; font-family: Calibri, Candara, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 10px;"> </p>
